ind":"gbp"},{"label":"GDP per head","value":33670,"year":"2023","kind":"gbp"},{"label":"Band D council tax (area bill)","value":2235.27,"year":"2026-27","kind":"gbp"},{"label":"Band D \u2014 council's own element","value":1724.76,"year":"2026-27","kind":"gbp"}]}},"dossier":{"summary":{"summary":"Brent's 2024/25 outturn shows external borrowing up \u00a385.8m (10.5%) to \u00a3900.0m, funding a capital programme that pushed the Loan CFR up \u00a3102.6m to \u00a31,357.1m (General Fund \u00a31,015.1m, HRA \u00a3342.0m). A \u00a313.7m budget variance on capital financing costs (\u00a341.5m actual against a \u00a327.8m budget) was offset by a drawdown from capital reserves. The council has grown related-party lending to its wholly-owned housing companies \u2014 \u00a3182.4m to I4B Holdings Ltd and \u00a333.8m to First Wave Housing \u2014 and holds \u00a359.5m of LOBO loans, of which \u00a335.0m face an interest-rate review in 2025/26.","fy":"2024/25","as_of_doc":"Treasury Management Outturn 2024/25","as_of_url":"https://democracy.brent.gov.uk/documents/s152292/15. Treasury Management Outturn 2024-25.pdf","as_of_date":"2025-09-08","signals":[{"code":"borrowing-increase","headline":"External borrowing rose \u00a385.8m (10.5%) to \u00a3900.0m in 2024/25, from \u00a3170.0m of new loans against \u00a384.2m of repayments.","why":"A rapid, double-digit rise in the debt stock within a single year."},{"code":"reserves-drawdown","headline":"A \u00a313.7m capital-financing budget variance (\u00a341.5m actual vs \u00a327.8m budget) was offset by drawing down capital reserves.","why":"Financing costs are already outrunning budget, absorbed by reserves rather than a revised budget."},{"code":"lobo-call-window","headline":"\u00a335.0m of the council's \u00a359.5m LOBO book (5 loans) is due an interest-rate review in 2025/26.","why":"If a lender exercises its option the council's own option is to repay at par, which is what councils do: every LOBO call we hold \u2014 Kent, Tameside, Newcastle, York, Barnet, Brighton and Hove, Bristol \u2014 was repaid rather than accepted. So the exposure is finding \u00a335.0m and replacing that funding at today's rates, not paying a higher rate on it."},{"code":"company-exposure","headline":"Loans to Brent's wholly-owned companies stood at \u00a3182.4m to I4B Holdings Ltd and \u00a333.8m to First Wave Housing at 31 March 2025, both secured on company property, plus a \u00a336.4m equity stake in I4B.","why":"Sizeable related-party credit exposure sits alongside the headline treasury debt figures."}],"key_figures":[{"name":"cfr","value":"\u00a31,357.1m total Loan CFR (General Fund \u00a31,015.1m, HRA \u00a3342.0m), up \u00a3102.6m in year","as_at":"31/3/2025","page":9},{"name":"borrowing total","value":"\u00a3900.0m, up \u00a385.8m (+10.5%)","as_at":"31/3/2025","page":2},{"name":"investments total","value":"\u00a347.3m cash investments, down from \u00a395.3m","as_at":"31/3/2025","page":2},{"name":"internal borrowing","value":"\u00a3457.1m","as_at":"31/3/2025","page":9},{"name":"lobo holdings","value":"\u00a359.5m total; \u00a335.0m (5 loans) due an interest-rate review in 2025/26; none repaid in 2024/25","as_at":"31/3/2025","page":7},{"name":"company lending","value":"\u00a3182.4m to I4B Holdings Ltd (secured on company property, \u00a35.3m interest received) and \u00a333.8m to First Wave Housing (secured, \u00a30.7m interest received); plus a \u00a336.4m equity stake in I4B","as_at":"31/3/2025","page":13},{"name":"maturity under 12m","value":"\u00a3130.5m of \u00a3900.0m (14.5%) matures within 1 year","as_at":"31/3/2025","page":7},{"name":"mrp","value":"\u00a319.8m total MRP charge (\u00a315.1m capital-programme borrowings, \u00a34.7m finance leases, \u00a30.9m service loans)","as_at":"2024/25","page":2},{"name":"treasury outturn vs budget","value":"Capital financing costs \u00a341.5m actual vs \u00a327.8m budget; \u00a313.7m variance offset by a drawdown from capital reserves","as_at":"2024/25","page":10}],"commercial":{"company_lending":{"value":"\u00a3182.4m to I4B Holdings Ltd (secured on company property, \u00a35.3m interest received) and \u00a333.8m to First Wave Housing (secured, \u00a30.7m interest received); plus a \u00a336.4m equity stake in I4B","as_at":"31/3/2025","page":13,"doc":"Treasury Management Outturn 2024/25"}},"tms_components":[{"key":"lobo_holdings","label":"LOBO loans (lender-option)","amount":59500.0,"detail":"\u00a359.5m total; \u00a335.0m (5 loans) due an interest-rate review in 2025/26; none repaid in 2024/25","as_at":"31/3/2025","page":7,"doc":"Treasury Management Outturn 2024/25"}]},"compliance":null,"documents":[{"title":"7bii. Appendix 2b - Prudential Indicators","url":"http://democracy.brent.gov.uk/documents/s158855/7bii-appendix-2b-prudential-indicators.pdf","committee":"Resources and Public Realm Scrutiny Committee","date":"29/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"7a. Appendix 1 - Financial Outturn 25-26","url":"http://democracy.brent.gov.uk/documents/s158852/7a-appendix-1-financial-outturn-25-26.pdf","committee":"Resources and Public Realm Scrutiny Committee","date":"29/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"7. Budget and Medium Term Financial Strategy Cover Report","url":"http://democracy.brent.gov.uk/documents/s158851/7-budget-and-medium-term-financial-strategy-cover-report.pdf","committee":"Resources and Public Realm Scrutiny Committee","date":"29/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"7c. Appendix 3 - Medium Term Financial Outlook","url":"http://democracy.brent.gov.uk/documents/s158856/7c-appendix-3-medium-term-financial-outlook.pdf","committee":"Resources and Public Realm Scrutiny Committee","date":"29/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"08d. Appendix 4- Prudential Indicators 2025.26 Outturn","url":"http://democracy.brent.gov.uk/documents/s158847/08d-appendix-4-prudential-indicators-2025-26-outturn.pdf","committee":"Audit and Standards Advisory Committee","date":"27/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"08a. Appendix A- Q1 Prudential Indicators 2026-27","url":"http://de